  "kind": "situation",
  "title": "Recover from an app-store rejection or removal",
  "summary": "A rejection names a guideline; a removal names a policy. Read which one you got. Apple publishes its App Review guidelines and an appeal path (disagreements go to the App Review Board); Google Play publishes its removal reasons and appeal process in the Play Console help. Usually, fixing the issue and resubmitting beats contesting, unless the reviewer is actually wrong about your app. If store revenue matters, tell your users what is happening while the review runs. How long review takes is the stores' call; treat it as a wait.",
